<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Gmyule</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>gmyule &lt;player&gt; &lt;kind of item&gt;&#160;: &lt;a line from Jolnir&gt;   (230)
gmyule &lt;player&gt; [clear]
gmyule list
</pre>
<p>The game master's reading of a player's Yule wish (see <a cmd='#'>Help Yule</a>). Players 
mail their wishes to the player Jolnir; a game master reads every letter a 
player sent and grants one gift with gmyule: the kind of item, as for 
<a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmtreasure</a> (long sword, ring, plate boots, any...), following the 
wish loosely, and a line Jolnir carves into it in runes.
</p><p>From December 24 to 31, when the player kneels before Jolnir, he makes the gift. 
Its quality is never the game master's: it is the rung of the player's level, an 
artifact from level 100, one lower with fewer than 24 spokes of the Yule Wheel, 
and nothing under 16. A player without a reading gets any kind.
</p><p>gmyule &lt;player&gt; shows what was recorded, clear removes it, and list shows them 
all. The readings are stored on disk, so a reboot keeps them.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmtreasure</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmquest</a>
</pre>




</div>